        "Author":  "dajoey",
        "Name":  "Gluttony Combo",
        "Punchline":  "Lalalazy fork of Wrath Combo — XIVCombo for very lazy players.",
        "Description":  "Gluttony Combo is a lalalazy-branded fork of Wrath Combo. Condenses combos and mutually exclusive abilities onto a single button — and then some. All upstream credit to Team Wrath / PunishXIV.",
        "InternalName":  "GluttonyCombo",
        "AssemblyVersion": "1.0.4.19",
        "Changelog": "v1.0.4.19 - Targeting loop during Pyretic finally fixed. Pyretic damage was already blocked in v1.0.4.17 but Gluttony autorotation kept running because the hardcoded NoActStatus ID list (960 / 1387 / 2127) missed the actual Pyretic variant in the latest dungeon. Run() kept swapping targets, AutoDuty cleared them, Run() swapped back - the fight Joey described.\n\nReplaced NoActStatus with Wrath upstreams PlayerHasActionPenalty at both gates (ShouldSkipAutorotation and UseActionDetour). PlayerHasActionPenalty builds the Pyretic lookup dynamically from Luminas status sheet by icon (215647) plus encounter-specific IDs plus Acceleration Bomb expiry-timing - same detection Wrath has shipped for months. Catches every Pyretic variant in every encounter without us having to maintain a hardcoded list.\n\nAlso cleaned up the duplicate \"using GluttonyCombo.Data;\" lines that the v1.0.4.17 patch script accidentally inserted ~25 times in AutoRotationController.cs (compiled fine but ugly).\n\nDeleted Data/NoActStatus.cs - superseded by PlayerHasActionPenalty.",
